From 8ae3af04f8b32de1cde1babe2ee2bc7a4f483bef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:29:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Evolution cancel: holding the cancel button stops an
 evolution the hours chose

While the old form is still on screen (the scene's tick below 0xcc) a ring with the cancel button's glyph and a
line (main.QOL_STR_EVO_CANCEL) sits in the bottom left corner. Holding the button for twenty ticks fills the
ring; released, it empties twice as fast. Full, the scene fades to black, gives back the camera, the palettes,
the map, the music and the old form's voices through its own state 3, and the field fades in with the partner
as it was. MOD_EVO_CANCEL (mod_qol.c) marks the evolutions that can be stopped (the ones rollNaturalEvolutionTarget
chose) and holds the hours' check until the partner's next sleep after a cancel. Evolutions by item, by the
praise-time rules and by the virus bar set no mark and show no ring.
---
 include/dw/mod_qol.h    |   7 ++
 src/evl/evl.c           | 164 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/main/mod_qol.c      |   6 ++
 src/main/partner.c      |   3 +
 src/main/partner_impl.c |  13 +++-
 text/main/mod_qol.yaml  |   3 +
 6 files changed, 188 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

